# Only PUBLISHED runs belong in the repository.
#
# A run writes wherever `--out` points, and while a strategy is being developed that is a dozen throwaway
# directories a day: smoke tests, one-conversation probes, sweeps, comparisons assembled by hand. Three
# separate commits have picked them up and had to be amended, because `git add benchmarks/` is the natural
# thing to type and there was nothing to stop it.
#
# So the rule is the NAME. A published run is a dated directory — `2026-09-06-tier0r-rank` — which is what
# the reports link to and what `README.md` cites. Anything else is working material and stays out.
#
# Consequence worth knowing: a new published run must be named this way or it is silently not committed.
# That is the failure direction chosen on purpose — a result missing from a commit is noticed when the link
# in the README does not resolve, whereas scratch output committed by accident is noticed by nobody.
*
!.gitignore
!20[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-*/
!20[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-*/**
